      "path": "docs/knowledge/why-clarify-split-into-clarify-discovery-and-exploring/why-clarify-split-into-clarify-discovery-and-exploring.md",
      "sourceId": "src_a8c0a5b0efee63da485942dabc98eec4",
      "identityStatus": "carried-forward",
      "sourceDigest": "b06349f25aa7eaf60e75331ba1d9f67eebc85e438f41f467e7b5dab15834363b",
      "blobSha": "71c00b05266fe39f417407457031a60ca58004f7",
      "blobSize": 26122,
      "area": "End-user authoring, index, and knowledge registry",
      "authorityStatus": "non-authority",
      "fileClass": "maintained-authority",
      "corpus": "user-knowledge",
      "switchboardSource": "scopedRoute",
      "gap": false,
      "documentType": null,
      "claimKind": "unclassified",
      "headingCount": 18,
      "unheadedBlockCount": 43,
      "mixedFileBlockCount": 0,
      "headings": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Why `clarify` split into `clarify`, `discovery`, and `exploring`",
          "anchor": "why-clarify-split-into-clarify-discovery-and-exploring",
          "githubAnchor": "why-clarify-split-into-clarify-discovery-and-exploring",
          "stableAnchor": "h-7af695c6fe8e"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The organizing principle: who is the author, not who approves",
          "anchor": "the-organizing-principle-who-is-the-author-not-who-approves",
          "githubAnchor": "the-organizing-principle-who-is-the-author-not-who-approves",
          "stableAnchor": "h-49d952d0dda0"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Why `clarify` stayed instead of being fully replaced",
          "anchor": "why-clarify-stayed-instead-of-being-fully-replaced",
          "githubAnchor": "why-clarify-stayed-instead-of-being-fully-replaced",
          "stableAnchor": "h-72621d173571"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The new `fgos-researching` skill: reusable, stage-agnostic, never self-aware of its caller",
          "anchor": "the-new-fgos-researching-skill-reusable-stage-agnostic-never-self-aware-of-its-caller",
          "githubAnchor": "the-new-fgos-researching-skill-reusable-stage-agnostic-never-self-aware-of-its-caller",
          "stableAnchor": "h-1bd586e0e075"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Why \"no available soul\" was ruled out as a real case",
          "anchor": "why-no-available-soul-was-ruled-out-as-a-real-case",
          "githubAnchor": "why-no-available-soul-was-ruled-out-as-a-real-case",
          "stableAnchor": "h-c512c64da4b1"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Reverting the verbs to pure write doors, and removing the judge subprocess from all three consumers",
          "anchor": "reverting-the-verbs-to-pure-write-doors-and-removing-the-judge-subprocess-from-all-three-consumers",
          "githubAnchor": "reverting-the-verbs-to-pure-write-doors-and-removing-the-judge-subprocess-from-all-three-consumers",
          "stableAnchor": "h-e2b5471f0633"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Migration: 57 open `clarify` items sorted by real signal, not touched uniformly",
          "anchor": "migration-57-open-clarify-items-sorted-by-real-signal-not-touched-uniformly",
          "githubAnchor": "migration-57-open-clarify-items-sorted-by-real-signal-not-touched-uniformly",
          "stableAnchor": "h-cb35821d47d3"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "A named, deliberately unresolved risk: could `clarify` and `exploring` re-merge in practice?",
          "anchor": "a-named-deliberately-unresolved-risk-could-clarify-and-exploring-re-merge-in-practice",
          "githubAnchor": "a-named-deliberately-unresolved-risk-could-clarify-and-exploring-re-merge-in-practice",
          "stableAnchor": "h-e20f8611d9d6"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "What stayed explicitly out of scope",
          "anchor": "what-stayed-explicitly-out-of-scope",
          "githubAnchor": "what-stayed-explicitly-out-of-scope",
          "stableAnchor": "h-a78fb8e22ccd"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Implementation (`tsk-1w7`, P4 of this design): why adding two stages didn't need a wider footprint",
          "anchor": "implementation-tsk-1w7-p4-of-this-design-why-adding-two-stages-didnt-need-a-wider-footprint",
          "githubAnchor": "implementation-tsk-1w7-p4-of-this-design-why-adding-two-stages-didnt-need-a-wider-footprint",
          "stableAnchor": "h-708f7877a858"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Implementation (`tsk-5mj`, P5 of this design): the runner dispatches `discovery` the same way it already dispatches `executing`",
          "anchor": "implementation-tsk-5mj-p5-of-this-design-the-runner-dispatches-discovery-the-same-way-it-already-dispatches-executing",
          "githubAnchor": "implementation-tsk-5mj-p5-of-this-design-the-runner-dispatches-discovery-the-same-way-it-already-dispatches-executing",
          "stableAnchor": "h-787430266e27"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Implementation (`tsk-1x3`, P3 of this design): `judge-executor.mjs` was deleted outright, not just unused",
          "anchor": "implementation-tsk-1x3-p3-of-this-design-judge-executormjs-was-deleted-outright-not-just-unused",
          "githubAnchor": "implementation-tsk-1x3-p3-of-this-design-judge-executormjs-was-deleted-outright-not-just-unused",
          "stableAnchor": "h-40282fcb58c1"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "`resolveDecompose` turned out asymmetric with `resolveDiscovery` (D16)",
          "anchor": "resolvedecompose-turned-out-asymmetric-with-resolvediscovery-d16",
          "githubAnchor": "resolvedecompose-turned-out-asymmetric-with-resolvediscovery-d16",
          "stableAnchor": "h-a2a87ca8bd92"
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "text": "`judgeVerifySemanticCorrectness` behaves differently from its two siblings (D17)",
          "anchor": "judgeverifysemanticcorrectness-behaves-differently-from-its-two-siblings-d17",
          "githubAnchor": "judgeverifysemanticcorrectness-behaves-differently-from-its-two-siblings-d17",
          "stableAnchor": "h-f4d385ccac96"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "A gap discovered later (`tsk-4b2`): despite this design, `discovery`/`exploring` were never actually reachable",
          "anchor": "a-gap-discovered-later-tsk-4b2-despite-this-design-discoveryexploring-were-never-actually-reachable",
          "githubAnchor": "a-gap-discovered-later-tsk-4b2-despite-this-design-discoveryexploring-were-never-actually-reachable",
          "stableAnchor": "h-e8b9bce9ec44"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Implementation (`tsk-4v6`, `tsk-4b2`'s own D5): the headless sweep gets the same verdict contract as the interactive path",
          "anchor": "implementation-tsk-4v6-tsk-4b2s-own-d5-the-headless-sweep-gets-the-same-verdict-contract-as-the-interactive-path",
          "githubAnchor": "implementation-tsk-4v6-tsk-4b2s-own-d5-the-headless-sweep-gets-the-same-verdict-contract-as-the-interactive-path",
          "stableAnchor": "h-2922020df830"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Implementation (`tsk-30v`): the edge choice itself finally reads the verdict, not just the stage",
          "anchor": "implementation-tsk-30v-the-edge-choice-itself-finally-reads-the-verdict-not-just-the-stage",
          "githubAnchor": "implementation-tsk-30v-the-edge-choice-itself-finally-reads-the-verdict-not-just-the-stage",
          "stableAnchor": "h-6c63fa51fc78"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The umbrella (`tsk-2mt`): six children, one parent branch, repeated sync friction",
          "anchor": "the-umbrella-tsk-2mt-six-children-one-parent-branch-repeated-sync-friction",
          "githubAnchor": "the-umbrella-tsk-2mt-six-children-one-parent-branch-repeated-sync-friction",
          "stableAnchor": "h-6c5e960d9930"
        }
      ],
