      "headings": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Why execution fan-out reuses `computeSchedule`, not `selectWave`, and stays a capability, not an entry point",
          "anchor": "why-execution-fan-out-reuses-computeschedule-not-selectwave-and-stays-a-capability-not-an-entry-point",
          "githubAnchor": "why-execution-fan-out-reuses-computeschedule-not-selectwave-and-stays-a-capability-not-an-entry-point",
          "stableAnchor": "h-ce2d098b61be"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Two distinct fan-out shapes, deliberately kept separate",
          "anchor": "two-distinct-fan-out-shapes-deliberately-kept-separate",
          "githubAnchor": "two-distinct-fan-out-shapes-deliberately-kept-separate",
          "stableAnchor": "h-88fd78309c9f"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Why children can just be dispatched as real work items — no new lifecycle-light category needed",
          "anchor": "why-children-can-just-be-dispatched-as-real-work-items-no-new-lifecycle-light-category-needed",
          "githubAnchor": "why-children-can-just-be-dispatched-as-real-work-items-no-new-lifecycle-light-category-needed",
          "stableAnchor": "h-11b1f3b89e3b"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Reusing `computeSchedule`, explicitly not `selectWave`",
          "anchor": "reusing-computeschedule-explicitly-not-selectwave",
          "githubAnchor": "reusing-computeschedule-explicitly-not-selectwave",
          "stableAnchor": "h-4ae87034be65"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Automated, but only for leaves — the root gate stays human, on purpose",
          "anchor": "automated-but-only-for-leaves-the-root-gate-stays-human-on-purpose",
          "githubAnchor": "automated-but-only-for-leaves-the-root-gate-stays-human-on-purpose",
          "stableAnchor": "h-6fba76e464a0"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Two topologies for \"children,\" resolved by reusing what already exists",
          "anchor": "two-topologies-for-children-resolved-by-reusing-what-already-exists",
          "githubAnchor": "two-topologies-for-children-resolved-by-reusing-what-already-exists",
          "stableAnchor": "h-277b6ec9b571"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Who claims, and why the parent never claims on a child's behalf",
          "anchor": "who-claims-and-why-the-parent-never-claims-on-a-childs-behalf",
          "githubAnchor": "who-claims-and-why-the-parent-never-claims-on-a-childs-behalf",
          "stableAnchor": "h-e7c11cc446ae"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "How results get collected: read state, don't trust a report",
          "anchor": "how-results-get-collected-read-state-dont-trust-a-report",
          "githubAnchor": "how-results-get-collected-read-state-dont-trust-a-report",
          "stableAnchor": "h-d194d424a750"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "A concurrency cap, and why it isn't the runner's own cap",
          "anchor": "a-concurrency-cap-and-why-it-isnt-the-runners-own-cap",
          "githubAnchor": "a-concurrency-cap-and-why-it-isnt-the-runners-own-cap",
          "stableAnchor": "h-47450af9f41d"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Fan-out is a capability, never a new entry point",
          "anchor": "fan-out-is-a-capability-never-a-new-entry-point",
          "githubAnchor": "fan-out-is-a-capability-never-a-new-entry-point",
          "stableAnchor": "h-dfb4511cc15d"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "A blocked sibling never cancels independent siblings",
          "anchor": "a-blocked-sibling-never-cancels-independent-siblings",
          "githubAnchor": "a-blocked-sibling-never-cancels-independent-siblings",
          "stableAnchor": "h-c4bb65bb69fa"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Verify proves real overlap, not just that a skill file exists",
          "anchor": "verify-proves-real-overlap-not-just-that-a-skill-file-exists",
          "githubAnchor": "verify-proves-real-overlap-not-just-that-a-skill-file-exists",
          "stableAnchor": "h-0239851a2939"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "A real friction hit at the `clarify → decompose` door",
          "anchor": "a-real-friction-hit-at-the-clarify-decompose-door",
          "githubAnchor": "a-real-friction-hit-at-the-clarify-decompose-door",
          "stableAnchor": "h-63d15ad9841b"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "What stayed deliberately unresolved for `fgos-coding-planning` to decide",
          "anchor": "what-stayed-deliberately-unresolved-for-fgos-coding-planning-to-decide",
          "githubAnchor": "what-stayed-deliberately-unresolved-for-fgos-coding-planning-to-decide",
          "stableAnchor": "h-af310960c6fd"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Follow-up finding (`tsk-4so`): the advisory verbs were already blind to any item not at `executing`",
          "anchor": "follow-up-finding-tsk-4so-the-advisory-verbs-were-already-blind-to-any-item-not-at-executing",
          "githubAnchor": "follow-up-finding-tsk-4so-the-advisory-verbs-were-already-blind-to-any-item-not-at-executing",
          "stableAnchor": "h-0486fbca69c1"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Implementation (`tsk-66d`): wiring fan-out into the shared anchor-report contract, not a new command",
          "anchor": "implementation-tsk-66d-wiring-fan-out-into-the-shared-anchor-report-contract-not-a-new-command",
          "githubAnchor": "implementation-tsk-66d-wiring-fan-out-into-the-shared-anchor-report-contract-not-a-new-command",
          "stableAnchor": "h-d95bb49fea64"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Implementation (`tsk-ik3`): `computeSchedule` gains an explicit candidate-set parameter",
          "anchor": "implementation-tsk-ik3-computeschedule-gains-an-explicit-candidate-set-parameter",
          "githubAnchor": "implementation-tsk-ik3-computeschedule-gains-an-explicit-candidate-set-parameter",
          "stableAnchor": "h-fd3a4576848b"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Companion fix (`tsk-4fg`, D3): `fgos list` needed a view lever, not a model change",
          "anchor": "companion-fix-tsk-4fg-d3-fgos-list-needed-a-view-lever-not-a-model-change",
          "githubAnchor": "companion-fix-tsk-4fg-d3-fgos-list-needed-a-view-lever-not-a-model-change",
          "stableAnchor": "h-9a9f81d35015"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Second companion fix (`tsk-59x`): leaf `cleanup` TTL should be short/zero, not the same 7 days as a root",
          "anchor": "second-companion-fix-tsk-59x-leaf-cleanup-ttl-should-be-shortzero-not-the-same-7-days-as-a-root",
          "githubAnchor": "second-companion-fix-tsk-59x-leaf-cleanup-ttl-should-be-shortzero-not-the-same-7-days-as-a-root",
          "stableAnchor": "h-602eba73a422"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Third companion fix (`tsk-1ug`): `fgos rollup` learns to read `targets`, not just `parent`",
