      "path": "docs/knowledge/why-status-splits-into-status-statuscategory-only-for-the-fr/multi-domain-status-category-schema.md",
      "sourceId": "src_7f8e0c227cf8a52f22c80da7585203db",
      "identityStatus": "carried-forward",
      "sourceDigest": "7cf21351c63b388bb6d6fdba95f7351fc3fbd3c632de2b97f81aa7dd60878048",
      "blobSha": "b2bf45fa5e5487a22c2fbdab75efe4f83f5c6768",
      "blobSize": 22451,
      "area": "End-user authoring, index, and knowledge registry",
      "authorityStatus": "non-authority",
      "fileClass": "maintained-authority",
      "corpus": "user-knowledge",
      "switchboardSource": "scopedRoute",
      "gap": false,
      "documentType": null,
      "claimKind": "unclassified",
      "headingCount": 16,
      "unheadedBlockCount": 38,
      "mixedFileBlockCount": 0,
      "headings": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Why status splits into status + statusCategory only for the front segment of the lifecycle",
          "anchor": "why-status-splits-into-status-statuscategory-only-for-the-front-segment-of-the-lifecycle",
          "githubAnchor": "why-status-splits-into-status-statuscategory-only-for-the-front-segment-of-the-lifecycle",
          "stableAnchor": "h-40847bf990a5"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The split only covers half the lifecycle, on purpose",
          "anchor": "the-split-only-covers-half-the-lifecycle-on-purpose",
          "githubAnchor": "the-split-only-covers-half-the-lifecycle-on-purpose",
          "stableAnchor": "h-4c944a6fa5c7"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Frozen at write time, never derived on read",
          "anchor": "frozen-at-write-time-never-derived-on-read",
          "githubAnchor": "frozen-at-write-time-never-derived-on-read",
          "stableAnchor": "h-4f8c5ef92317"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "`domainFields` follows the same \"additive, not a redesign\" shape",
          "anchor": "domainfields-follows-the-same-additive-not-a-redesign-shape",
          "githubAnchor": "domainfields-follows-the-same-additive-not-a-redesign-shape",
          "stableAnchor": "h-76cc9aed2ce6"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "What this design deliberately did not solve",
          "anchor": "what-this-design-deliberately-did-not-solve",
          "githubAnchor": "what-this-design-deliberately-did-not-solve",
          "stableAnchor": "h-e06caa526da4"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Outcome",
          "anchor": "outcome",
          "githubAnchor": "outcome",
          "stableAnchor": "h-cadb9a9cfbb6"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The decision record itself narrowed the scope it formalizes",
          "anchor": "the-decision-record-itself-narrowed-the-scope-it-formalizes",
          "githubAnchor": "the-decision-record-itself-narrowed-the-scope-it-formalizes",
          "stableAnchor": "h-9086f762df4a"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The schema field itself landed as its own narrow child task",
          "anchor": "the-schema-field-itself-landed-as-its-own-narrow-child-task",
          "githubAnchor": "the-schema-field-itself-landed-as-its-own-narrow-child-task",
          "stableAnchor": "h-0785de2b4955"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The backfill migration (D4) needed two retries before it verified clean",
          "anchor": "the-backfill-migration-d4-needed-two-retries-before-it-verified-clean",
          "githubAnchor": "the-backfill-migration-d4-needed-two-retries-before-it-verified-clean",
          "stableAnchor": "h-cebdd865ccf2"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Consumer migration closed the `RESOLVED_STATUSES` gap the audit flagged",
          "anchor": "consumer-migration-closed-the-resolved_statuses-gap-the-audit-flagged",
          "githubAnchor": "consumer-migration-closed-the-resolved_statuses-gap-the-audit-flagged",
          "stableAnchor": "h-822515021ee6"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The `skillMap.retrospective` key (D5) is what `/fgOS:retro-next` reads today",
          "anchor": "the-skillmapretrospective-key-d5-is-what-fgosretro-next-reads-today",
          "githubAnchor": "the-skillmapretrospective-key-d5-is-what-fgosretro-next-reads-today",
          "stableAnchor": "h-7b63af26b9eb"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "`domainFields` (D6) landed as a thin, narrowly-verified addition",
          "anchor": "domainfields-d6-landed-as-a-thin-narrowly-verified-addition",
          "githubAnchor": "domainfields-d6-landed-as-a-thin-narrowly-verified-addition",
          "stableAnchor": "h-393769b9d701"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The fixture domain proving the design (`tsk-38t-7`), last child to land",
          "anchor": "the-fixture-domain-proving-the-design-tsk-38t-7-last-child-to-land",
          "githubAnchor": "the-fixture-domain-proving-the-design-tsk-38t-7-last-child-to-land",
          "stableAnchor": "h-449e53dc4c63"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The `herdr-plugin` literal-status dependency, later actually removed — once new evidence existed",
          "anchor": "the-herdr-plugin-literal-status-dependency-later-actually-removed-once-new-evidence-existed",
          "githubAnchor": "the-herdr-plugin-literal-status-dependency-later-actually-removed-once-new-evidence-existed",
          "stableAnchor": "h-3799f13d5112"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The stale triage-table doc gap (`tsk-38t-8`) — independent of the category decision",
          "anchor": "the-stale-triage-table-doc-gap-tsk-38t-8-independent-of-the-category-decision",
          "githubAnchor": "the-stale-triage-table-doc-gap-tsk-38t-8-independent-of-the-category-decision",
          "stableAnchor": "h-372dce943d52"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The `herdr-plugin` gap the audit flagged, resolved by pinning the current behavior rather than migrating it",
          "anchor": "the-herdr-plugin-gap-the-audit-flagged-resolved-by-pinning-the-current-behavior-rather-than-migrating-it",
          "githubAnchor": "the-herdr-plugin-gap-the-audit-flagged-resolved-by-pinning-the-current-behavior-rather-than-migrating-it",
          "stableAnchor": "h-c7114361a1c4"
        }
      ],
